  "id": "COMPOUND:36702 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "Rubrenolide is implicated in the regulation of Histone H1.0 through its interaction with NQO1 protein, which serves as a common target across multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Rubrenolide modulates NQO1, a key enzyme involved in DNA repair and detoxification processes, and that this modulation ultimately leads to the targeting of Histone H1.0. The diverse molecular structures of the targets—ranging from a naphthalene derivative to a cyclohexyl acetic acid—highlight the complexity of the interaction network, yet all converge on NQO1 as a central mediator. The consistent presence of NQO1 as a target in all three paths underscores its role in the drug's mechanism, while the varied chemical structures suggest that Rubrenolide may interact with NQO1 through different binding modes or post-translational modifications. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Rubrenolide exerts its effects on Histone H1.0 via NQO1, potentially influencing chromatin structure and function.",
